// # sec/pqc/mlkem/ — ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203)
//
// Logline: Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism. Keygen,
// Encaps, Decaps. First-party PQC, fail-closed.
//
// Setup: Domain module. Caps and layout are in the parent ANCHOR.oo.
//
// Beats:
//   1. mlkem.c — orchestrator: ML-KEM-768 keygen/encaps/decaps.
//   2. mlkem_internal.c — FIPS 203 NTT + sampling + byte conversions (the algorithm core).
//   3. mlkem_kem.c — the KEM primitives (Encaps/Decaps key derivation).
//
// v3.1.0 file split: the original 520-line mlkem.c was split into the
// mlkem/ subdir (3 files). The mlkem_internal.c (460 lines) is the
// algorithm core that stays over 256 by design — the FIPS 203 NTT,
// sampling, and polynomial arithmetic are tightly coupled; splitting
// them would fragment the algorithm without a functional boundary.
//
// ──▓▓ sec/pqc/mlkem ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: PQC-by-default — first-class in the runtime ::
